# Settings kit

Every Management page uses the components in
`Packages/OsaurusCore/Views/DesignSystem`. `SettingsKitGallery` (Debug:
Developer Tools → Server → Settings Kit Gallery, or its `#Preview`) shows each
one in every state. Pick from there before writing UI.

| Need | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Page | `SettingsPage { SettingsPageHeader(…) } content: { … }` |
| Group of rows | `SettingsSection` (Title Case title, one flat group; direct children become rows) |
| Row | `SettingsToggle`, `SettingsPickerRow`, `SettingsValueRow`, `SettingsLinkRow`, `SettingsNavigationRow`, `SettingsRow`, `SettingsAbilityRow`, `SettingsDestructiveRow`, `SettingsPermissionRow` |
| Value control in a row | `SettingsMenuPicker` (native pop-up), `SettingsSearchablePicker` (long lists: search, groups, keyboard), `SettingsPopUpButton` (opens a popover picker), `SettingsStepper` / `SettingsStepperRow`, `SettingsSliderRow` |
| Text input | `SettingsFieldRow` + `SettingsTextField` / `SettingsTextEditor`; `SearchField` for search |
| Button | `SettingsButton`, `SettingsIconButton`, or `.buttonStyle(.settings(role, size:))` |
| Menu of actions | `SettingsOverflowMenu` (icon only, ⋯ by default), `SettingsMenuButton` (titled, Import ▾) |
| Page notice | `SettingsCallout` |
| Metrics / status | `SettingsStatStrip` (`.divided` headline numbers, `.tiles` live readings), `SettingsStatusHero` (the page's one live value + state + action) |
| Explainer | `SettingsFeatureCards` (`.leading` above a page; `.centered` is the hero empty state's examples) |
| Check results | `SettingsFindingRow` (preflight, doctor, inspector rows: severity glyph, title, code/value, detail, fix) |
| Label / count | `StatusChip`, `CountBadge` |
| Filter | `FilterChipRow`, `FilterChip`, `FilterTokenChip` |
| Grid / list item | `LibraryCard`, `LibraryRow`, `LibraryIcon` |
| Comparable collection (sortable columns, row opens a detail panel) | `SettingsDataTable` + `SettingsDataTableColumn` (width, sort key, hide priority) |
| Pushed page | `SettingsBackBar` / `SettingsSubPageBar` + `SettingsDetailHeader` |
| Empty / loading | `SettingsEmptyState` (hero, `inline:`, `loading:`), `SettingsSkeletonBar` + `.settingsShimmer()`, `SettingsProgressBar` |
| Surface | `.settingsChrome(.card / .control / .inset / .selected / …)` |
| Type | `SettingsFont.*` (add `.weight` / `.italic()` / `.monospacedDigit()` as needed) |

Rules:

- No hand-drawn chrome: no `RoundedRectangle(...).fill(theme…)`, no
  `Capsule().fill` pills, no padded plain-style buttons, no raw `TextField` /
  `SecureField` / `TextEditor`, no `.font(.system(size:))` on text, no
  uppercased or tracked titles. Every `Toggle` carries `.settingsSwitch()` or
  `.settingsCheckbox()`.
- One-of-few choices are a segmented `Picker` (or `SettingsPickerRow`), not a
  row of custom buttons. A value picked from a list is `SettingsMenuPicker`;
  never a custom-label `Menu` with a hand-drawn chevron.
- Never `.menuStyle(.borderlessButton)` with a custom label: macOS drops the
  label's background and tint, leaving a bare accent glyph. Menus go through
  `SettingsOverflowMenu` / `SettingsMenuButton` (`.menuStyle(.button)` with a
  kit button style).
- Rows inside any card or surface draw flat (`.settingsChrome` sets
  `settingsInGroup`), so never wrap a row in its own card inside a group.
- Section and row titles are Title Case ("Swap Local Models for Subagents");
  descriptions, captions and button labels are sentence case. Header refresh is
  `SettingsIconButton("arrow.clockwise")`, never a text "Refresh" button.
- Inner navigation is one of two kinds, never both on a page:
  - `SettingsTabsRow` in the header when the views are peers over one
    collection (scopes or kinds of the same list: Local Models kinds,
    Plugins, Skills, Insights).
  - `SettingsDrillInHost` + `SettingsDrillInRows` when the children are
    different kinds of page (Memory, Voice, Privacy, Server, Computer &
    Browser Use). Drill-in ids are stable deep-link keys.
- Animation respects `accessibilityReduceMotion`.
- Need a variant the kit lacks? Extend the kit component, add it to the
  gallery, and migrate callers. Do not fork a private copy.
- Kit text parameters are catalog keys unless the parameter says it is
  already localized or a `verbatim` flag is set.

`SettingsKitLintTests` scans every non-chat view. Component rules are at zero;
a new violation fails the test. The token rules (`rawPadding`, `rawRadius`,
`rawFixedWidth`: literal numbers where a `theme.space` / `theme.radius`
token or kit component belongs) carry per-file counts that only go down:
adding a literal fails, and removing one fails until you lower the baseline
with `SETTINGS_KIT_LINT_WRITE_BASELINE=1 swift test --filter SettingsKitLintTests`.
`SettingsKitLintBaseline.allowlist` exempts specific
rules for surfaces that are not settings rows (chat-shared views, sidebar,
tables, artwork) and must only shrink. Do not add a file to it to silence a
new violation.

```swift
// BAD
Text(status).font(.system(size: 10, weight: .semibold))
    .padding(.horizontal, 6).padding(.vertical, 2)
    .background(Capsule().fill(Color.green.opacity(0.15)))

// GOOD
StatusChip(status, tone: .success)
```
